<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zedekiah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">reigned 597–587 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zedekiah was the last king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judah">Judah</a>, placed on the throne by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nebuchadnezzar-ii">Nebuchadnezzar II</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> in 597 BCE. When he rebelled with Egyptian encouragement, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonians">Babylonians</a> besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>, which fell in 587 or 586 BCE. According to the Bible he was captured near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jericho">Jericho</a>, forced to watch his sons killed, blinded and taken in chains to Babylon.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zedekiah.jpg" alt="Zedekiah" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Guillaume Rouille · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zedekiah.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
